# Tailscale ACL — Client Isolation Pattern

## Rule

One-direction only: w-alter → clients. Clients cannot initiate ANYTHING.

```jsonc
{
    "acls": [
        {
            "action": "accept",
            "src":    ["tag:w-alter"],
            "dst":    ["tag:w-alter-clients:22", "tag:w-alter-clients:5900"]
        }
    ],
    "tagOwners": {
        "tag:w-alter":         ["autogroup:admin"],
        "tag:w-alter-clients": ["autogroup:admin"]
    }
}
```

## Effect Matrix

| Initiateur      | Cible               | Résultat |
|-----------------|---------------------|----------|
| w-alter         | Client Mac (SSH/VNC)| ✅ OK    |
| Client Mac      | w-alter             | ❌ Bloqué |
| Client Mac      | User's Mac          | ❌ Bloqué |
| Client Mac      | Any tailnet node    | ❌ Bloqué |
| Client Mac      | Internet            | ✅ OK (hors tailnet) |

No rule for `tag:w-alter-clients` → anything = deny by default.
The client can only reply to established connections; it never opens new ones.

## Auth Key Generation

1. admin.tailscale.com → Settings → Keys → Generate auth key
2. Ephemeral: YES
3. Tag: `tag:w-alter-clients`
4. Share key with friend (paste into script on first launch)
